    "rationale": "Correct: expanding the left side gives the right side for every value of x."
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "content": "$2x + 3 = 7$",
    "rationale": "This is an equation, true only when x = 2."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "$x^{2} = 4x$",
    "rationale": "This is an equation, true only when x = 0 or x = 4."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "$(x + 2)^{2} = x^{2} + 4$",
    "rationale": "False in general: $(x + 2)^{2} = x^{2} + 4x + 4$, so this holds only when $x = 0$."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "An identity is true for every value of the variable; an equation is true only for particular values.",
